  "_comment": "Square corners up onto the high mesa, a chicane between rock pillars, then into the mesa itself: a rock tunnel that climbs inside the rock and bursts out onto the rim, straight into a long glide back down to the canyon floor, an off-camber drop and rocks tumbling across the floor. A dry gulch cuts inside the chicane while boulders drop into it in turn, updraft vents blow along the canyon floor every few seconds, and from lap 2 rockfalls narrow the climb to the mesa.",
